 highlight  so we can share that it's not all about  roses but we have some torns as well  along the way  uh definitely uh we definitely hit our  share of challenges um  i would say that most of them are  were around working with nexjs which  especially when we were getting started  was a relatively new uh javascript  framework and had a fairly small  community of developers that were  deploying it uh to google cloud  our original application used app engine  that was the first thing that i thought  of to deploy next js um because it was  super easy to set up you know we had it  up in like an hour  but uh one of next js's most exciting  features is incremental static  regeneration that allows us to  statically generate content at build  time and then when updates happen have  them regenerate without having to  redeploy  the thing is if your regenerating static  content you need to be able to write it  to disk and app engine doesn't do that  so uh we had an issue where we were you  know scratching our heads and saying  why isn't this content updating like you  know and it actually had led to a 404  because we had moved something from one  page to another page and we were like  why are these four fours happening  and uh then we realized that it's a  read-only file system so uh to fix that  issue we moved our application to google  cloud run there was a thankfully a  pretty simple tool to auto generate the  config for cloud run from an app engine  app and uh we were redeployed in a few  hours and we've been on that happily  ever since  but uh yeah it was a little scary in the  moment to be like wait a minute we have  to change our server deploying platform  like that that's gonna take forever but  it ended up being uh  simpler than we had originally thought  so  looking to the future  then what are any technical enhancements  or anything that is your own your  roadmap  planned for  for for the future  yeah uh two big ones come to mind the  first is task queues uh as i 